<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greece</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greece is a region in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> on the Balkan peninsula and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands, the home of ancient Greek civilisation. It was the target of Achaemenid invasions, came under Macedonian dominance, and was contested by Hellenistic powers including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>. In later periods it was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, and in the twentieth century it was invaded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greece.jpg" alt="Greece" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Greece.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
